- **`signer.py` others:** Hsiaoming Yang has 10 lines (3.7%) and Arnout van Meer has 8 (3.0%). Both are inactive.
- **`timed.py` others:** Zach Hugnou has 4 lines (1.7%) and Alan Hamlett has 3 (1.3%). Both are inactive.
- **Activity marker:** "Active" means a commit in the year before 2025-07-08. I did not use it to change the order.
- **Why David Lord first:** On `signer.py` he is inactive (last commit 2024-04-16). He is still the top owner by lines, so ask him anyway. If he doesn't answer, Tomás Ibarra is the active owner.
- **Armin Ronacher:** He is the original author. 116 of his lines (10.8%) survive package-wide, but he has not committed since 2018. I would not ask him.

**Caveats**
- **Bus factor:** It is 1 on the whole package, on `signer.py` and on `timed.py`. In each case David Lord alone holds more than 50% of the surviving lines. Reaching 80% takes 2 authors in each scope. Bus factor here means the fewest authors whose surviving lines reach 50% of the lines counted.
- **Reformat commit ignored:** `ffeab7f` ("[pre-commit.ci] auto fixes", 2025-07-08) only changed whitespace and quotes. The table leaves it out. Counting it would give David Lord 713 lines (68.4%) instead of 741.
- **Bots:** `pre-commit-ci[bot]` is excluded, and its lines are not credited to anyone.
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked them. The package-wide run set aside 1 commit, the reformat commit above. The `signer.py` and `timed.py` runs set aside none, and no other commit looks mechanical.
- **Copy detection:** The figures use `-w -M -C`.
  - Package-wide, David Lord has 741 lines (69.2%) with it and 854 (79.7%) without. Armin Ronacher has 116 (10.8%) with it and 24 (2.2%) without.
  - On `signer.py`, David Lord has 162 lines (59.8%) with it and 190 (70.1%) without.
  - On `timed.py`, David Lord has 142 lines (60.4%) with it and 166 (70.6%) without.
  - Some of Armin Ronacher's share comes from code that was moved into these files, mostly from the old `itsdangerous.py` and `__init__.py`. About 11% of each file was written elsewhere and moved in. Credit goes to the people who wrote those lines, not to whoever moved them.
- **Identity merging:** No duplicate identities were found, and there is no `.mailmap`.
- **Deleted legacy module:** Gustavo Reyes added `legacy.py` in July 2025, and David Lord deleted it. None of it survives, so Gustavo Reyes holds no lines.
- **Limits:** Line counts say whose code remains. They say nothing about quality, design work or review.
